# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, and Lane M is native Windows.
# Without this file, its clone checks out index.html (~1MB, one line region per
# iframe srcdoc) as CRLF. Committing through git normally converts back to LF, so
# the common path survives -- but this setup moves files by scp/rsync/SSH heredoc
# too, and any of those lands CRLF in the repo and produces a whole-file diff that
# Lane E, as sole release engineer, then has to merge. Pin it explicitly rather
# than depending on every machine's git config being right.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Clip media must never be line-ending-converted. Git's NUL-byte heuristic already
# classifies these binary, but the app's whole media pipeline runs across two
# operating systems now, so state it rather than rely on detection.
*.mp4  binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary

# Keep the shell entry point LF even if a future .gitattributes generalises: a
# CRLF shebang line makes the script unrunnable with a confusing "bad interpreter".
*.sh   text eol=lf
